# The keys of [pme] for the prolate kernel (D266): what belongs
# to the other kernel is refused, not ignored, and so is an order of the
# window outside 5 to 8, and a tolerance that the automatic grid cannot meet.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/opc/opc.prmtop %S/Inputs/opc/opc.inpcrd %t
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %s | sed '1d;$d' > %t/base.toml
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/kernel = "PROLATE"\nbeta = 0.35/' %t/base.toml > %t/beta.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/beta.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BETA
# BETA: 'beta' is for kernel = "GAUSSIAN"
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/kernel = "PROLATE"\ninfluence = "OPTIMAL"/' %t/base.toml > %t/influence.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/influence.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=INFLUENCE
# INFLUENCE: 'influence' is for kernel = "GAUSSIAN"
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/bandwidth = 12.0/' %t/base.toml > %t/bandwidth.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/bandwidth.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BANDWIDTH
# BANDWIDTH: 'bandwidth' is for kernel = "PROLATE"
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/window_bandwidth = 12.0/' %t/base.toml > %t/window.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/window.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WINDOW
# WINDOW: 'window_bandwidth' is for kernel = "PROLATE"
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/kernel = "PROLATE"\norder = 4/' %t/base.toml > %t/order4.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/order4.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ORDER4
# ORDER4: expected 5, 6, 7, or 8 points of the window for 'order' with kernel = "PROLATE"
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/order = 5/' %t/base.toml > %t/order5.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/order5.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ORDER5
# ORDER5: expected 4, 6, or 8 for 'order'
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/kernel = "ELLIPTIC"/' %t/base.toml > %t/kernel.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/kernel.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=KERNEL
# KERNEL: expected one of GAUSSIAN, PROLATE for 'kernel', got 'ELLIPTIC'
# A tolerance that the aliasing estimate of the window does not reach
# below half of it on twice the grid of eq. 15: refused, with what to do.
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/kernel = "PROLATE"\ntolerance = 1e-9\norder = 8/' %t/base.toml > %t/floor8.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/floor8.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FLOOR8
# FLOOR8: the aliasing estimate of the prolate kernel with 8 points of the window stays above half the tolerance 1e-09 of [pme] on every grid: it is {{.*}} at {{[0-9]+}} x {{[0-9]+}} x {{[0-9]+}} points, twice the grid of eq. 15, and falls only slowly beyond it, toward the floor that the tail of the window sets; 8 points are the most; give a looser 'tolerance', or the grid in 'grid'
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/kernel = "PROLATE"\ntolerance = 1e-9\norder = 5/' %t/base.toml > %t/floor5.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/floor5.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FLOOR5
# FLOOR5: with 5 points of the window stays above half the tolerance 1e-09 of [pme] on every grid: {{.*}}; give more points of the window in 'order' (up to 8), a looser 'tolerance', or 'grid'

# The B-spline window (D[prolate-bspline-grid]): a tolerance that its mesh
# error estimate does not reach on eight times the grid of eq. 15: refused.
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/kernel = "PROLATE"\ncontinuity = 2\ntolerance = 1e-9/' %t/base.toml > %t/spline.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/spline.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SPLINE
# SPLINE: the mesh error estimate of the prolate kernel with the B-spline window stays above its bound 1e-09 for the tolerance 1e-09 of [pme]: it is {{.*}} at {{[0-9]+}} x {{[0-9]+}} x {{[0-9]+}} points, 8 times finer than the grid of eq. 15; give a looser 'tolerance' or the grid in 'grid'{{$}}
# With 'bandwidth' alone the default tolerance 1e-5 is the bound, which
# c = 9.5392 does not reach there.
# RUN: sed 's/^#PME$/kernel = "PROLATE"\ncontinuity = 2\nbandwidth = 9.5392/' %t/base.toml > %t/spline-bandwidth.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t/spline-bandwidth.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SPLINE-BANDWIDTH
# SPLINE-BANDWIDTH: stays above its bound 1e-05 for the tolerance 1e-05 of [pme]: {{.*}}; give a looser 'tolerance' or the grid in 'grid' ('tolerance' sets this bound also when 'bandwidth' is given)

